{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a visible-light-promoted enantioselective conjugate addition of alpha-silylamines to alpha,beta-unsaturated carbonyl compounds using a single, earth-abundant Ni(II)-DBFOX complex as a bifunctional catalyst. The nickel complex acts as both a photoredox catalyst to generate alpha-aminoalkyl radicals and a chiral Lewis acid to control the stereochemistry of the radical addition, yielding chiral gamma-amino carboxylic acid derivatives and gamma-lactams with high enantioselectivity (80-99% ee).",
